  <h3 class="linklist">1940s Bolex Catalogs</h3>
  <!-- GENERIC multiple use small item descriptions Lenses Accessories and Ephemera -->
  <div id="books"> 
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/ephemera/40cat001.jpg" alt="Bolex 1939 Catalog" width="176" height="259"></li>
      <li class="title"><strong>Better Pictures With Bolex</strong></li>
      <li class="author">American Bolex Company</li>
      <li><strong>Content:</strong> 24 pages; cardboard cover</li>
      <li><strong>Year:</strong> 1939</li>
      <li><strong>Language:</strong> English</li>
      <li class="desc">This is an early catalog from the American Bolex Company, 
        the sole distributor of Bolex cameras and all Paillard products in the 
        US during the 1930s and '40s. It contains mostly text and art illustration, 
        with only two actual photographs, and discusses the features of the H-16, 
        Model G projector and Hugo Meyer lenses. The introduction notes the history 
        of Paillard and focuses on Swiss craftsmanship as a selling point. </li>
    </ul>
    <hr class="spacer">
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/ephemera/40cat002.jpg" alt="Bolex 1940 Catalog" width="175" height="242"></li>
      <li class="title"><strong>Better Pictures With Bolex</strong></li>
      <li class="author">American Bolex Company</li>
      <li><strong>Content:</strong> 36 pages</li>
      <li><strong>Year:</strong> 1940</li>
      <li><strong>Language:</strong> English</li>
      <li class="desc">All of the content from the previous catalog is featured 
        here; it's expanded, however, with more photos and the addition of a few 
        Ambol accessories and the H-8. The cover, in mint condition, is glossy 
        and textured; it also contains a price list insert. </li>
    </ul>
    <hr class="spacer">
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/ephemera/40cat003.jpg" alt="Bolex 1941 Catalog" width="174" height="242"></li>
      <li class="title"><strong>Better Pictures With Bolex</strong></li>
      <li class="author">American Bolex Company</li>
      <li><strong>Content:</strong> 48 pages</li>
      <li><strong>Year:</strong> 1941</li>
      <li><strong>Language:</strong> English</li>
      <li class="desc">This catalog lists many accessories from Paillard, Cinea, 
        Ambol and other manufacturers, in addition to discussing the features 
        and specifications of the H-16, H-8 and Model G projector. Like most American 
        Bolex Company catalogs, a separate price list was included. </li>
    </ul>
    <hr class="spacer">
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/ephemera/40cat004.jpg" alt="Bolex Spiral Catalog" width="174" height="243"></li>
      <li class="title"><strong>Better Pictures With Bolex</strong></li>
      <li class="author">American Bolex Company</li>
      <li><strong>Content:</strong> 48 pages; Spiral bound</li>
      <li><strong>Year:</strong> 1941</li>
      <li><strong>Language:</strong> English</li>
      <li class="desc">I've only seen one of these, and here it is. I can't be 
        certain, but it appears to be a dealer or shop catalog, maybe for in-store 
        reference. It is spiral bound, and includes both a retail price list and 
        a separate "Dealer Discount Sheet and Price List". Otherwise, it's similar 
        to the blue catalog, but with additional accessories listed. </li>
    </ul>
    <hr class="spacer">
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/ephemera/40cat005.jpg" alt="Bolex Bulletin" width="200" height="259"></li>
      <li class="title"><strong>Bolex Mail Order Bulletin</strong></li>
      <li class="author">American Bolex Company</li>
      <li><strong>Content:</strong> 16 pages</li>
      <li><strong>Year:</strong> 1942</li>
      <li><strong>Language:</strong> English</li>
      <li class="desc">This magazine-sized booklet announces a new mail-order 
        service from the American Bolex Company and advertises some of the photographic 
        products and accessories offered. It also introduces a lower price for 
        the Bolex H8 or H16 at $191, Excise Tax included; a bargain, compared 
        to the former price of $283 US! </li>
    </ul>
    <hr class="spacer">
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/ephemera/40cat006.jpg" alt="Bolex World's Finest" width="174" height="246"></li>
      <li class="title"><strong>The World's Finest Movie Cameras</strong></li>
      <li class="author">American Bolex Company</li>
      <li><strong>Content:</strong> 65 pages</li>
      <li><strong>Year:</strong> 1946</li>
      <li><strong>Language:</strong> English</li>
      <li class="desc">The 1946, 1947 and 1948 American Bolex Company catalogs 
        have identical covers, except for the date printed on each. These catalogs 
        were updated with photos and details of the latest cameras, lenses and 
        accessories; a separate sheet listing current retail prices was included. 
      </li>
    </ul>
